{"title":"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the maximum number of points of intersection of the graphs of two different fourth degree polynomial functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1db541df4771c9ef32bf4a78b920414c112e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/6575f2613b4ad59ee0ac9cf2be663373151e1834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />, each with leading coefficient 1?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/eca9c199457b3a969c269d3a518c50570d72f108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The intersections of the two polynomials, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/5/2751d79d3bbfb34440d68c685fe6ba7414951749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b5f855b56cd269cd617940805cef31bc41a95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, are precisely the roots of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/0665674fd7907c7bddfe5b4fc98ce4f1f20dfb81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x)=q(x) \\rightarrow p(x) - q(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />. Since the leading coefficients of both polynomials are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the degree of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f5c4092a4e1c64c0a82862772ffe7d94fa171e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x) - q(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> is at most three, and the maximum point of intersection is three, because a third degree polynomial can have at most three roots. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME\" title=\"1999 AHSME\">1999 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\